<title>USA: TABLE-Giant Industries Q2 shr $0.51 vs $0.77.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Giant Industries Q2 shr $0.51 vs $0.77.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ar. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.51		    $0.77</p>
<p> Net			  5,675		    8,621</p>
<p> Revs		     154,123		  135,643</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  11,071		   11,260</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.61		    $0.96</p>
<p> Net			  6,799		   11,025</p>
<p> Revs		     270,261		  239,743</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  11,084		   11,256</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company reported operating income for the quarter of $12.8 million compared with $17.3 million.</p>
<p>The company reported a net loss from discontinued operations of $72,000 in the 1996 quarter.</p>
<p>The company said its second quarter earnings this year were hurt by a four week major maintenance turnaround at its Bloomfield refinery and the &quot;dramatic&quot; decline in West Coast product prices.</p>
<p>It also said its purchase of 96 service stations/convenience stores from Thriftway Marketing Corp and the acquisition of Phoenix Fuel Co Inc were completed late in the quarter and had little impact on earnings.</p>
<p>Giant Industries Inc.</p>
</text>
